INT. DRAGON'S TOOTH MINE - DEEP SHAFT - DAY

Black rock veined with ivory. Lanterns hang from iron hooks. The walls are warm.

ALDRETH (40s, foreman, leather vest, pickaxe on his shoulder) squints into the dark. PIP (12, mine boy, soot-faced, torch held two-handed) grips his sleeve. MARN (30s, miner, huge arms, a sledge) swings at the vein, stone chips flying. YSABEAU (20s, mapmaker, ink on her nose, a roll of parchment under her arm) taps a compass.

The wall exhales. Hot breath, sulfur-yellow. Every lantern bows.

PIP
Foreman?

ALDRETH
Nobody move.

Marn lowers the sledge. Ysabeau closes the compass. Pip ducks behind Aldreth. Together they back up into the narrow shaft as the vein of ivory glows orange and the stone around it begins to crack like an egg.

A figure steps out of the dark behind them. GORRAN (60s, a wyrm-warden, scaled leather armor, a staff of blackened bone) taps the floor once. The cracking stops.

GORRAN
You've dug into the nursery.

ALDRETH
We didn't know.

GORRAN
Few do. Put down the picks. Back out, slowly, and thank the mountain it's sleeping.

Marn drops the sledge. Ysabeau bows. Pip, trembling, holds out his torch, and Gorran takes it, and pinches the flame out with two bare fingers.
